# Relay reads provider credentials from the environment. Copy this file to
# `.env` (already git-ignored) and fill in real values, or export the variables
# in your shell. Relay never writes credentials to project state, artifacts,
# logs, or the fact store.

# Which variables Relay reads is configuration: each provider connection in
# relay.config.yaml names its variable with `apiKeyEnv`. The defaults:
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Additional Anthropic Messages-compatible connections name their own
# variable with `apiKeyEnv` in relay.config.yaml (for example a gateway
# connection with a `baseUrl`), e.g.:
# GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# Anthropic Messages is Relay's only live external model protocol; the
# offline `fake` connection needs no credentials. The `openai-chat` adapter
# was removed — see docs/configuration.md for the migration error obsolete
# configurations produce.
